regardless of politics I think we can  all agree that those photos of Ronald  Reagan driving around his ranch in the  80s are pretty iconic his dope jeeps are  what make the shot but try to drive one  of those now and the maintenance and odd  mechanics won't make it easy that's why  I was happy to try out a new scrambler  of sorts the one made by two mechanics  in Wyoming who started a company called  legacy power wagons together they've  been building this type of wagon for  more than 40 years  I wanted to see if this Jeep drives as  great as it looks so I took it out to  the orange groves near Ojai California  both on the road and up the side of the  neighboring Hills  now since this aluminum truck is so  light at only 3,200 pounds and capable  with more than a dozen variations of  high neutral or low drive for both front  and rear wheels it can handle everything  from boulders and sand to rivers and  snow  when he put it into first low gear it  practically walks itself down the hill  like a big animal crawling over the  rocks this $150,000 new old truck packs  a 240 horsepower Boeing military diesel  engine housed in a badger tank and it  gets a massive 420 foot-pounds of torque  basically right from the get-go  the one I drove is a six-speed Automatic  but you can choose to have a manual  version as well it's the ideal estate  car or safari wagon  feel like you're in the same animal that  is like  have to drive it but it's not great for  highway driving or cruising around town  it's just too loud and bumpy you'll  arrive looking like a tornado blew you  in but it does feel pretty amazing to  drive like you're in the war rig with  furiosa herself it rumbles like a tank  and is towering Lehigh with massive  brakes and a steering wheel that goes  all over the place enough to give to  forge a minefield did I mention the fuel  efficiency in this thing is more than 30  miles per gallon  that's better than plenty of luxury  sedans and sports cars better yet the  scrambler comes with a soft top and  totally customizable seat options for  the rear and everything inside including  the seats and the radio are treated to  be waterproof interested the waiting  list is a year long and it takes nearly  another year to build legacy makes only  10 or so of these a year and they sell  out really quickly so you'll have to be  patient but that's ok good things take  time  especially good all american-made things  Reagan would be proud
 

